# Staging only (never the shipped release): lets the on-device test suite run against the R8 build.
# The test APK is rewritten with the app's R8 mapping, so renaming (obfuscation) is still tested;
# what tests can't survive is removal of code the app itself doesn't use. So for staging:
# - keep the androidx.test runtime pieces that live in the app APK,
# - keep app classes from being removed or reshaped, but let R8 rename them as in release.
-keep class androidx.tracing.** { *; }
-keep,allowobfuscation class io.github.drjkn7.shoestep.** { *; }
# The test APK also uses library code the app doesn't (Kotlin, coroutines, Compose test hooks):
# keep it whole (the Compose test toolkit breaks if coroutines are renamed). Library shrinking and
# removal of unused app code are checked on the real release APK by the release smoke test.
-keep class kotlin.** { *; }
-keep class kotlinx.** { *; }
-keep class androidx.** { *; }
